    {
      "title": "Rubio urges India to boost US energy, defence buys amid strained ties",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/economy/news/india-is-a-refining-superpower-can-process-venezuelan-oil-marco-rubio-126102000549_1.html",
      "description": "US Secretary of State Marco Rubio on Tuesday described India as a refining superpower, adding that the US delegation will discuss with Reliance about producing oil in Venezuela.\nAsked what role India can play in meeting the world's energy demand, Rubio, who arrived in Mumbai this afternoon on a three-day India visit, said, \"India is a refining superpower. They have the capability to refine heavy crude. They've done so in the past, and I think as more and more Venezuelan oil comes online, it's something they can do.\"\n\"They also, by the way, have pre-existing oil concessions in Venezuela that can produce more themselves,\" Rubio told reporters in Mumbai.\nHe said all these are positive things.\n\"I'm not claiming to you that Venezuela alone can fill the hole that could be caused by some of the things that are happening around the world, but I think over time, it most certainly can, and in the short term, it can certainly help.\n\"So, that's one of the things we'll talk about. With India,",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-20T12:00:40"
    },
    {
      "title": "Rubio begins India visit, to hold crucial talks with Jaishankar in Mumbai",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/external-affairs-defence-security/news/rubio-begins-india-visit-to-hold-crucial-talks-with-jaishankar-in-mumbai-126102000134_1.html",
      "description": "US Secretary of State Marco Rubio will begin his three-day visit to India on Tuesday to advance bilateral ties in energy, trade and investment, defence, critical technologies, and exchange views on the West Asia crisis.\nRubio's second India visit this year comes amid persistent friction in bilateral ties.\nDuring his earlier trip in May, he held talks with Prime Minister Narendra Modi and External Affairs Minister S Jaishankar, besides attending a Quad foreign ministers' meeting.\nThe US Secretary of State is expected to be accompanied by a large business delegation, and his October 20-22 trip is likely to focus largely on boosting India-US economic engagement.\nIn their meeting in Mumbai on Tuesday afternoon, Jaishankar and Rubio are expected to deliberate on ways to further strengthen the India-US Comprehensive Global Strategic Partnership.\nRubio is scheduled to land at Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj International Airport at 2.15 pm, according to the Ministry of External Affairs ...",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-20T04:52:49"
    }
